      "notes": "The House on Grisewood is a horror game and contains sustained frightening content.\r\n\r\nViolence and gore: The player uses firearms against humanoid supernatural enemies. Combat produces visible blood spatter, pooling blood on the floor, and blood trails tracked underfoot. Enemies are depicted as emaciated, disfigured human figures. There is no dismemberment or graphic anatomical detail, and the art style is low-resolution and stylized rather than photorealistic.\r\n\r\nHorror and startle content: The game is played almost entirely in darkness with a limited flashlight, and is designed around sudden appearances of enemies at close range. It contains jump scares, screen-shake, brief red screen flashes when the player is injured, and distressing audio including screaming, crying, laughter, and breathing. Players sensitive to sudden loud noise or abrupt visual shifts should be aware of this.\r\n\r\nThemes: The setting involves a haunted house, death, and the implied deaths of previous occupants. The player character can die, and death is depicted on screen.\r\n\r\nThe game does not contain sexual content or nudity, sexual violence, drug or alcohol use, self-harm, suicide, or violence against children. There is no profanity."
